# TestBed: Angular's Test Environment

`TestBed` creates a module specifically for testing. It lets you configure a testing module with the component, its dependencies, and any providers you want to mock.

```typescript
TestBed.configureTestingModule({
  declarations: [MyComponent],
  providers: [MyService]
}).compileComponents();
```

After configuration, you can create the component fixture: `TestBed.createComponent(MyComponent)`.

slides.codeSnippet:
// app-title.component.ts
@Component({ template: '<h1>{{ title }}</h1>' })
class AppTitleComponent { title = 'Hello'; }

// app-title.component.spec.ts
describe('AppTitleComponent', () => {
  let fixture: ComponentFixture<AppTitleComponent>;
  beforeEach(() => {
    TestBed.configureTestingModule({ declarations: [AppTitleComponent] });
    fixture = TestBed.createComponent(AppTitleComponent);
  });
  it('should display title', () => {
    fixture.detectChanges();
    const h1 = fixture.nativeElement.querySelector('h1');
    expect(h1.textContent).toContain('Hello');
  });
});

