Components often depend on services. Instead of using the real service (which might make HTTP calls), provide a **mock**.

```typescript
const mockService = jasmine.createSpyObj('MyService', ['getData']);
mockService.getData.and.returnValue(of('mock data'));

TestBed.configureTestingModule({
  providers: [{ provide: MyService, useValue: mockService }]
});
```

Now the component gets a fake service, and you control its return values.

slides.codeSnippet:
describe('CalculatorService', () => {
  let service: CalculatorService;
  beforeEach(() => { service = new CalculatorService(); });

  it('should add two numbers', () => {
    expect(service.add(2, 3)).toBe(5);
  });

  it('should subtract two numbers', () => {
    expect(service.subtract(5, 2)).toBe(3);
  });
});
